1
00:04:36,774 --> 00:04:42,774
Some assembly required.

2
00:09:13,548 --> 00:09:19,548
The Avengers is a science fiction, action,
adventure film directed by Joss Whedon.

3
00:13:50,322 --> 00:13:56,322
When an unexpected enemy emerges and threatens global safety and security, Nick Fury, director of the international peacekeeping
agency known as S.H.I.E.L.D., finds himself in need of a team to pull the world back from the brink of disaster.

4
00:18:27,096 --> 00:18:33,096
Spanning the globe, a daring recruitment effort begins!

5
00:23:03,870 --> 00:23:09,870
Tony Stark / Iron Man, played by Robert Downey Jr..

6
00:27:40,645 --> 00:27:46,645
Steve Rogers / Captain America, played by Chris Evans.

7
00:32:17,419 --> 00:32:23,419
Bruce Banner / The Hulk, played by Mark Ruffalo.

8
00:36:54,193 --> 00:37:00,193
Thor, played by Chris Hemsworth.

9
00:41:30,967 --> 00:41:36,967
Natasha Romanoff / Black Widow, played by Scarlett Johansson.

10
00:46:07,741 --> 00:46:13,741
Clint Barton / Hawkeye, played by Jeremy Renner.

11
00:50:44,516 --> 00:50:50,516
Marvel's The Avengers (titled Marvel Avengers Assemble in the United Kingdom and Ireland and commonly referred to as simply
The Avengers) is a 2012 American superhero film based on the Marvel Comics superhero team of the same name.

12
00:55:21,290 --> 00:55:27,290
Produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Walt Disney Studios Motion
Pictures, it is the sixth film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

13
00:59:58,064 --> 01:00:04,064
Written and directed by Joss Whedon, the film features an ensemble cast including Robert Downey Jr., Chris Evans, Mark Ruffalo, Chris
Hemsworth, Scarlett Johansson, and Jeremy Renner as the Avengers, alongside Tom Hiddleston, Stellan Skarsgård, and Samuel L.

14
01:04:34,838 --> 01:04:40,838
In the film, Nick Fury and the spy agency S.H.I.E.L.D.

15
01:09:11,612 --> 01:09:17,612
recruit Tony Stark, Steve Rogers, Bruce Banner, Thor, Natasha Romanoff, and Clint Barton to
form a team capable of stopping Thor's brother Loki from subjugating Earth.

16
01:13:48,387 --> 01:13:54,387
The film's development began when Marvel Studios received
a loan from Merrill Lynch in April 2005.

17
01:18:25,161 --> 01:18:31,161
After the success of the film Iron Man in May 2008, Marvel announced that The Avengers would be released in July 2011 and would bring together Stark (Downey),
Rogers (Evans), Thor (Hemsworth), and Banner (portrayed by Edward Norton in the 2008 film The Incredible Hulk) from Marvel's previous films.

18
01:23:01,935 --> 01:23:07,935
After the signing of Johansson as Romanoff in March 2009, Renner as Barton in June 2010, and Ruffalo
to replace Norton as Banner in July 2010, the film was pushed back for a 2012 release.

19
01:27:38,709 --> 01:27:44,709
Whedon was hired in April 2010 and rewrote the original screenplay by Zak Penn.

20
01:32:15,483 --> 01:32:21,483
Production began in April 2011 in Albuquerque, New Mexico, before moving to
Cleveland, Ohio, in August and New York City in September.

21
01:36:52,258 --> 01:36:58,258
The film has more than 2,200 visual effects shots.

22
01:41:29,032 --> 01:41:35,032
The Avengers premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Los Angeles on April 11, 2012, and was
released in the United States on May 4, as the final film in Phase One of the MCU.

23
01:46:05,806 --> 01:46:11,806
The film received praise for Whedon's direction and screenplay, visual
effects, action sequences, acting, and musical score.

24
01:50:42,580 --> 01:50:48,580
It grossed over $1.5 billion worldwide, setting numerous box office records and becoming the
third-highest-grossing film of all time at the time of its release and the highest-grossing film of 2012.

25
01:55:19,354 --> 01:55:25,354
It was the first Marvel production to generate $1 billion in ticket sales.

26
01:59:56,129 --> 02:00:02,129
In 2017, The Avengers was featured as one of the 100 greatest
films of all time in an Empire magazine poll.

27
02:04:32,903 --> 02:04:38,903
It received a nomination for Best Visual Effects at the 85th
Academy Awards, among numerous other accolades.

28
02:09:09,677 --> 02:09:15,677
Three sequels have been released: Avengers: Age of Ultron (2015),
Avengers: Infinity War (2018), and Avengers: Endgame (2019).

29
02:13:46,451 --> 02:13:52,451
The film explores themes of new york city, superhero,
shield, based on comic, alien invasion.

30
02:18:23,225 --> 02:18:29,225
The tone is thought_provoking.
